Subject: webui: release callbacks, report failures and save uname safely
Upstream-Status: Pending [sidex15/susfs4ksu-module; its WebUI sources are not published, so this patches the minified bundle]
Drop-when: upstream ships these fixes; until then redo it on every release, whose bundle name and identifiers change

Commands reuse the counter-based callback allocator; rejections and
synchronous bridge exceptions release the callback, and dependent
initialization and uname updates wait for completion. Uname saving uses
one operation for manual values and the stock build date, escaping shell
arguments, shell configuration values and sed replacements separately;
NUL and line breaks are rejected. The config reader decodes that
quoting. Cached and displayed values change only after a successful
save, the save buttons are disabled while saving and failures are
reported. Covered by workspace/tests/module/module.test.cjs.
